# CODEOWNERS — required reviewers for sensitive files
# Syntax: <pattern> <owner> [<owner>...]
# Owners are notified when matching files are changed in a PR.
# See: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# AUDIT-INFRA-06 (audit 2026-03-15): .secrets.baseline is a detect-secrets
# suppression list. Any change must be reviewed by the repository owner to
# prevent contributors from hiding newly-committed secrets in the baseline.
.secrets.baseline @egorribun

# CI/CD workflow changes affect the entire security posture of the project.
.github/workflows/ @egorribun
/.github/scripts/ @egorribun

# Scanner policy, ignore lists and dependency allowlists directly influence
# required security checks. Keep both the policy files and this ownership
# boundary itself under repository-owner review (SEC-CI-02/03).
/.github/CODEOWNERS @egorribun
/.github/codeql/ @egorribun
/.github/actionlint.yaml @egorribun
/.github/dependency-review-config.yml @egorribun
/.checkov.yml @egorribun
/.semgrep.yml @egorribun
/.semgrepignore @egorribun
/.pre-commit-config.yaml @egorribun
/.trivyignore @egorribun
